	(text_box "Gate driver design notes\n\n- INA/INB - Logic input with TTL compatible thresholds and internal pull-down resistor.\n- VDDI - Input-side supply voltage: Range 3 V to 17 V\n- DIS - Disable input channel A and B (active High, DIS high causes OUTA/OUTB low).\n- STP/DTC - Shoot-through protection and dead time control. If STP/DTC is HIGH or open, OUTA and OUTB can overlap. If STP/DTC is connected to GNDI with a resistance RDTC"
